# 📌 What is Linux?

Linux is a free and open-source operating system kernel created by Linus Torvalds in 1991. Over time, the Linux kernel became the foundation for complete operating systems known as **Linux distributions (distros)**.

A Linux distribution combines:
- Linux kernel
- GNU utilities
- Package manager
- Desktop environment (optional)
- Additional software

## Popular Linux Distributions

- Ubuntu
- Debian
- Fedora
- Red Hat Enterprise Linux (RHEL)
- CentOS Stream
- Arch Linux
- Kali Linux
- Parrot OS

## Why Linux is Popular

- Open-source and community-driven
- Stable and reliable
- Secure by design
- Lightweight and efficient
- Highly customizable
- Runs on almost any hardware
- Dominates server and cloud environments

