# 🧩 Key Characteristics of Linux

## 1. Open Source
The source code is publicly available, allowing anyone to inspect, modify, and distribute it.

## 2. Multi-user
Multiple users can use the system simultaneously.

## 3. Multitasking
Many programs and processes can run at the same time.

## 4. Portable
Runs on desktops, servers, smartphones, routers, and embedded devices.

## 5. Secure
Provides:
- File permissions
- User/group isolation
- Firewall support
- Logging and auditing

## 6. Modular
Components such as the shell, package manager, and desktop environment can be changed independently.

