# ☁️ Linux in Cloud Computing

Linux powers most of the internet and cloud infrastructure.

## Cloud Service Models

### IaaS (Infrastructure as a Service)
Provides virtual machines, storage, and networking.

Examples:
- AWS EC2
- Azure Virtual Machines
- Google Compute Engine

### PaaS (Platform as a Service)
Provides managed application platforms.

Examples:
- Google App Engine
- Azure App Service
- Heroku

### SaaS (Software as a Service)
Ready-to-use software delivered over the web.

Examples:
- Gmail
- Microsoft 365
- Slack

## Why Linux Dominates the Cloud

- Low resource usage
- Excellent networking support
- Strong security
- Automation-friendly
- Open-source ecosystem

